    "title": "Secret Agent",
    "description": "Secret Agent is a song I have been working on for decades. I always felt that it was one of my most complete and mature songs involving lots of chord changes, tempo changes and style changes mid song. I imagined a spy reflecting on his life, remembering near death encounters and always returning to some sleezy bar and ordering a cliché Martini.\r\nThis version is very cinematic and quite different to the version I recorded in the 1980s in terms of production and instrumentation. But it’s close to how I imagined the song when I first wrote it. Talent and resources limited the demo I originally produced!\r\n\r\nStyles:\r\n\r\nrap, orchestral hip-hop, cinematic, chorus should be sung by raw male vocal, heroic, electric guitar, melodic piano, ‑choir\r\n\r\nAudio Influence 55%",
    "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\r\n\r\nI wonder out of a smokey bar \r\nin a darkened street with a burnt out car\r\nThe gentle caress of a warm breeze\r\nmovement in the darkness as I find my keys\r\ninto my car but I'm not alone\r\n\"Don't touch that gun\", “it's just my comb”\r\nHis face I know, that scar was a gift\r\nFrom our last encounter in a glass lift\r\n“Let me comb my hair was my last request”\r\n“You're gonna meet your maker, you gotta look your best”\r\nFrom the comb came a flash and a tiny dart\r\nStraight through his jacket and pierced his heart\r\n\r\n[Instrumental]\r\n\r\n[Chorus] \r\n\r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\n\r\n[Verse 2]\r\n\r\nI'm locked in a room and the waters coming in\r\nThe level's getting higher so I start to swim\r\nI reach into my pocket and i pull out my pen\r\nThere's a small breathing device hidden within\r\nSomethings in here with me and it brushes past my leg\r\nI don't know what it is but i think it's pretty big\r\nWith the wire in my watch I tie one end to the door\r\nThe creature swims towards me where I'm waiting on the floor\r\nI throw my watch into it's mouth\r\nIt tries to follow as i swim to the roof\r\nThe door swings open and the water rushes out\r\nNow i wonder how I'm gonna get the creases out my suit.\r\n\r\n[Instrumental]\r\n\r\n[Chorus] \r\n\r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\nOn the rocks, shaken not stirred\r\nThat's what I want\r\nThat's what I deserve \r\n\r\n[Outro]\r\nOn the rocks\r\nOn the rocks\r\nOn the rocks",
    "mp3": "mySongs/mp3/Secret Agent.mp3",
