    "id": "the-way-i-feel",
    "title": "The Way I Feel",
    "description": "The Way I Feel is a classic failed romance song, he is a gambler and she thought she could change him. That rarely works!  The song builds both instrumentally, vocally and emotionally and I class this version as one of my best. It’s good old story telling in a song, something I really like, something with a start, middle and end.\r\nThis version is quite different to my original recording I made in the late 80’s. My original version was very much a pop song with lots of jangly guitars but it never really conveyed the emotion of the protagonist. This version really hits home as it builds towards the end.\r\n\r\nStyles\r\n\r\nElectric Guitar, Acoustic Guitar, Electric Bass Guitar, Drums, harmonies\r\nWeirdness 40%\r\nStyle Influence 40%",
    "lyrics": "[Intro]\r\n\r\n[Verse 1]\r\n\r\nI still don’t understand why you went away\r\nLeft me alone on a stormy day\r\nYou packed up your bags and left, me alone\r\nYou walked out and left me and our happy home\r\n\r\n[Verse 2]\r\n\r\nI’ve seen you act so different just recently\r\nYou tell me that it’s Sunday when it’s Saturday\r\nI thought we’d be together for a long, long time\r\nBut you treat me like I’ve committed some awful crime\r\n\r\n[Bridge]\r\n\r\nWell I told you once and I told you twice\r\nI just can’t be what you want me to be\r\nI can’t resist the roll of a dice\r\nBut it doesn’t change\r\nThe way I feel\r\nThe way, I feel, about you\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\nAh ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\nAh ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\n\r\n[Verse 3]\r\n\r\nI thought you knew exactly just where we stood\r\nYou day you moved in you told me that you could\r\nLive with a man who, loved the risk\r\nYou knew that gambling was always on the list\r\n\r\n[Verse 4]\r\n\r\nSo I don’t wanna hear it that you thought I would change\r\nI know that’s the reason why you’re acting so strange\r\n‘Cause there can’t be another reason why you would leave\r\nNothing I can think of that I’m ready to believe\r\n\r\n[Instrumental]\r\n\r\n[Bridge]\r\n\r\nWell I told you once and I told you twice\r\nI just can’t be what you want me to be\r\nI can’t resist the roll of a dice\r\nBut it doesn’t change\r\nThe way I feel\r\nThe way, I feel, about you\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\nAh ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\nAh ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\n\r\n[Verse 5]\r\n\r\nStill don’t understand why you went away\r\nYou left me alone on a stormy day\r\nYou packed up your bags and left me alone\r\nYou walked out and left me and our happy home\r\n\r\n[Verse 6]\r\n\r\nSo come back now ‘cause I miss you so much (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\nI miss your style and I miss your touch (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\n‘Cause I can’t stand another moment living on my own (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\nListen to me darling please come straight back home (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\n\r\n[Instrumental]\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\nAh ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\nAh ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah (Ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah ah ah, ah)\r\n\r\n[Outro]\r\n\r\n[End]",
